> > Has anyone tried modifying Nethack's seeding of the RNG?
> 
> What's the point? If you want to play the same game twice, it won't work
> unless you arrange matters so that the same pseudo-random numbers in the
> sequence are used for the same purposes; the only way that you're likely
> to achieve this is giving identical input.



An interesting possibility for seeding the RNG is to have the game record 
your RNG seed and all of your keystrokes. At the end of the game, it could 
write out to a file the seed and keys. You could then send that to a 
friend, who could run nethack in a "replay" mode, with the sent file as 
input, and he could watch your entire game played out.

	% nethack -replay <replayfile> -speed <keys/second>

There would need to be a few other params in the replay file, such as date
and time of the game (for moon/midnight effects), and the windowing
backends would need to know not to take ANY key/mouse inputs (e.g. <MORE>)
during replay mode.


